From 6afb49bf48361a257bad31c3acecff0de547a19d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resource-packs): resolve licensed native image fallbacks

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 protocol 2193 accepts Hive item atlas aliases to vanilla images which the server does not resend. The bundled metadata archives intentionally contain no images, leaving these aliases unresolved during Java conversion.

Expose a platform provider for licensed image-only resource layers. Acquire them on the existing pack executor and wait alongside the server download without blocking its Netty event loop. Preserve native overlay precedence below bundled metadata and server packs, include their exact pixels in conversion cache fingerprints, and keep them outside server advertisements and pack identity tracking.

Native equipment can refer to built-in geometry, animations, controllers
and material parents. Permit these actor dependency documents from the
licensed provider while keeping them below server packs. Do not publish
unrelated block or entity definitions. Permit only the exact item and
terrain atlas paths needed for native icon selection. The synthetic shield
regression covers dependencies, server precedence and provenance.

Permit the exact native textures/item_texture.json and textures/terrain_texture.json atlases alongside licensed images. Its definitions are necessary to select built-in item sprites without server overrides.

Load an optional verified native-image bundle from the core classpath when
a platform does not supply its own image library. ViaProxy otherwise
converts accepted attachables without their inherited native inventory
images and falls back to held geometry in GUI contexts. The same authored
BDS pack shows blank proxy icons while the direct route has an image
provider. Preserve server priority, atlas aliases, path casing and numeric
vanilla overlay order rather than changing item identity or held models.

The build derives only images and the two native atlases from the existing
checksum-verified Bedrock 1.26.51.1 source archives. Validate the packaged
manifest, target protocol, per-file hashes, bounds, and layer order before
constructing lower-priority packs. A missing optional bundle preserves the
existing empty provider; a malformed present bundle fails explicitly.
The source images and generated bundle stay outside Git.

Regression coverage includes default item icon conversion with retained
held selectors, server image and atlas overrides, original bytes and path
case, numeric/base overlay order, invalid manifests and immutable lists.
The StackAnvil build verifies the exact bundle in core and both consumers.
This supplies the same native image fallback on proxy and direct routes;
it does not establish complete native visuals or other actor semantics.
